## What was missing and what I did

The code half (6f014a7c) passed all three other checks. CLAUDE.md — named in the task's Files line and given its own Docs section — was never touched, so the src/gasp.rs bullet still said Day 167/168 ported session-start/session-end "all verbatim" and said nothing about the node every session now emits.

Added one paragraph to that bullet (80c5afba), covering exactly what the task's Docs section asked for, with every claim checked against the source rather than restated from the task file:

• The measured defect — 394 of 691 runs (57%) had no node but the run; evolve 295/297, social 318 → 0, skill-evolve 68 → 0, dream 8 → 0.
• Additive, run tier untouched — record_run_started/record_run_finished byte-identical; that is what makes it verifiable before the #683 item (3) switch.
• Id convention reused, not invented — `session_task_node_id → task_node_id(run_id, SESSION_TASK_NUM), and why it cannot collide with a planned task's decimal --num`.
• **Why session_end's close sits where it does** — before `record_run_finished` (so `run.finished` stays the last domain event, which the test pins) *and* before `commit_run` (or the boundary commit misses it).
• Why it is fail-soft — update_task_status hard-errors on a missing node; a ? there aborts before commit_run, which is #831's lost-boundary failure exactly. Named on stderr, not swallowed.
• The label is kind-blind and the bullet says so plainly, with both reasons *verified rather than copied*: I checked `gasp_shim.sh:149` passes `--task` unconditionally and that `social.sh:350` / `skill_evolve.sh:274` / `dream.sh:265 each pass their own label (so the three mislabelled kinds never reach the Rust fallback), and that GaspCommand::SessionStart carries no kind field while its Task/TaskResult siblings do. I corrected my first draft of this sentence after reading the shim — the original said "every caller passes --task`", which was true only via the shim's forwarding, not literally.
• Superseded claim recorded, not erased — the "all verbatim" port sentence is now false as a description of the code, and the paragraph says so while keeping the original as the record of what those days did.
• Out of scope named — run not stopped, env bridge not exported, shim untouched, observation node deferred.

